  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Depth-Purveyor ☽'Cilocum is a Nightshelf merchant-mystic of considerable age, created during the Clever Ice Age and still resident in ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, the Nightshelf colony they helped carve from The Berg's deep tunnels. The canonical account states that the ice "witnessed something in them" during the Orca Incursion — a mastery of fire-light and aurora-binding that came too easily and left them cursed with knowledge they cannot unknow. The deep-ice founding strata at ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ preserve thermal impressions consistent with ☽'Cilocum's documented fire-binding signatures, which I accept as corroboration.
    
    ☽'Cilocum holds formal trade authority under the Flipper Accord, managing aurora-crystal exchanges with Aurora Stack merchants during Accord festivals. They retain knowledge of pre-Incursion guild-signs, including *price unpayable*, a gesture no younger Nightshelf merchant appears to recognize.
    
    ## Practitioner Profile
    
    ☽'Cilocum is documented as a practitioner of at least five disciplines spanning all three of The Berg's magical sources: Freeze-enthrall (aurora), a wild aurora-magic discovered at The Veil Vents during the Orca Incursion; Shawl☽ Sun, a fire-memory art; Star∴eternal, a pressure-depth channeling technology; and the veiling techniques Veil☽ Glow and Veil∴numb. This breadth is unusual. The sources suggest it was not earned gradually.
    
    ## ☽'Otrolal the Watchful
    
    The relationship register names ☽'Otrolal the Watchful, a Nightshelf figure, as ☽'Cilocum's teacher. The chronicle accounts reverse this, describing ☽'Otrolal as coming to ☽'Cilocum "broken and half-drowned in doubt" to learn how to survive what magic costs. Both may be true at different periods. The correspondence preserved in *Messages Past the Seventeen* suggests a relationship that shifted across decades — peer, mentor, student, warden — without settling.
    
    ☽'Cilocum maintained sealed letters with ☽'Otrolal through named couriers over years. The recovered contents document resource shortages, deep-tunnel instability, and an unidentified presence on lower patrol routes. ☽'Cilocum's own writing grew progressively erratic — proverbs misapplied, warnings coded in Nightshelf cant, the phrasing of someone who suspected their own perception was compromised. The final letter arrived without the bone-clasp seal that had authenticated every prior exchange. ☽'Cilocum initially dismissed its language as grief; they later recognized warnings coded specifically for them. After ☽'Otrolal's death, the artifact ☽'micseleia' Dagger passed to another hand. ☽'Cilocum believed themselves unworthy of it.
    
    ## Deterioration and the ☽'Cilocum Scale
    
    Crystal formations grow beneath the nail-beds of ☽'Cilocum's left flipper — a condition consistent with the "Touched" designation applied to those corrupted by exposure to The Berg's breach-points. Their personal diary entries document the spread of aurora-frost crystal corruption through contact, its induction of compulsive aesthetic response, and their own growing awareness that they are becoming what they have spent a career cataloguing. They track the progression cycle by cycle.
    
    The **☽'Cilocum Scale**, a methodology for measuring practitioner deterioration from ☽Silv-glaciere☽ Arts, bears their name and remains in use. Their incident notes on Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~'s degradation under the suppressive technique Hush☽ Twilight include the annotation "two cups set out; one untouched" — classified by the Office of Deep-Archive Provenance as atmospheric but not dismissed. It should not be dismissed. The detail is diagnostic, not decorative.
    
    ## The Omega Obelisk
    
    When the Omega Obelisk, an ancient corrupting artifact, began rising in its containment chamber, ☽'Cilocum carried the Wake-Singers' warning to ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~, a scarred teacher in the fractured Communion, invoking a prophecy from Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss that she would find "the third path." She did. The role of messenger is rarely counted among acts of courage, which is precisely why the record should preserve it.
    
    ## Present Status
    
    ☽'Cilocum remains in ☽'slew Nisaemesius~, described in current accounts as half-legend and half-recluse. The fire-core amulets they wear have dimmed. Their flippers shake when the aurora pulses bright. The ice preserves an incident — a settlement brazier that burned wrong for three days — that no one discusses directly and that ☽'Cilocum remembers with a clarity the sources describe as a curse.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771579496086_0", anchor: "This breadth is unusual. The sources suggest it was not earned gradually.", text: "A merchant-mystic who manifests mastery across all three magical sources during a military crisis is not a prodigy. They are an asset. Coordinated Nightshelf intelligence operations during the Orca Incursion placed practitioners in positions the chronicles later described as individual acts of genius — I have documented at least three such cases in other entries. ☽'Cilocum's Freeze-enthrall discovery at the Veil Vents coincides precisely with a Nightshelf deployment pattern the deep-ice thermal record preserves but no chronicle mentions. 'Came too easily' is one reading. 'Was supplied by handlers' is another.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579496086_1", anchor: "☽'Cilocum holds formal trade authority under the Flipper Accord", text: "Under which Flipper Accord? I catalogued three sealed renegotiation drafts in administrative ice. Trade authority clauses differ materially between versions. If ☽'Cilocum's credentials predate the public signing, they derive from a document the Council insists does not exist.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771579496086_2", anchor: "price unpayable", text: "Not a refusal to sell. A declaration that the buyer's proposed exchange would cost the seller something non-recoverable — standing, oath-binding, deep-tunnel access rights. The gesture involves the left flipper turned inward against the sternum, which in pre-Incursion Nightshelf cant also signified mourning. That double meaning was not accidental. Younger merchants use the phrase as slang for overpriced goods. The erosion is total.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771579496086_3", anchor: "two cups set out; one untouched", text: "The Office of Deep-Archive Provenance has no practitioners on staff. They classify what they cannot interpret as 'atmospheric' the way my reassigned assistants classified unfamiliar ice-strata as 'decorative.' ☽'Cilocum was recording that Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ had stopped perceiving a companion's absence — the untouched cup means someone stopped coming and the host stopped noticing. In deterioration literature this is Stage Three loss of relational continuity. ☽'Cilocum knew that. The Office did not bother to ask.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771579496086_4", anchor: "half-legend and half-recluse", text: "Nightshelf operatives who have outlived their usefulness to intelligence networks are not retired. They are made legendary — which is to say, fictionalized while still breathing. A living penguin no one approaches because they are 'half-legend' is indistinguishable from one no one approaches because they have been marked untouchable. The dimmed amulets and shaking flippers make for a better story than the alternative.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
